Description: Wild OS first run
 The seven first run steps. In the first boot setup session (wildos-setup)
 it sets the region and language, joins Wi-Fi and makes the account, then
 plans the rest for that account: taskbar layout and accent colour, copying
 documents, photos, music and bookmarks from a Windows drive on the same
 computer, the privacy choices, and the Windows programs found there, with
 their Store replacements or fresh installers and Windows mode's licence
 check. An account made later sees the last four steps at its first
 sign-in.
